routed.text:
To find the simple (arithmetic) average, add the four figures together and then divide by 4.

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Sum} &= 1.1\text{M} + 1.3\text{M} + 1.25\text{M} + 1.4\text{M} \\
           &= 5.05\text{M} \\
\text{Average} &= \frac{5.05\text{M}}{4} \\
               &= 1.2625\text{M}
\end{aligned}
\]

**Average revenue:** **\$1.2625 million** (≈ \$1.263 M).

Earnings per share (EPS) is calculated by dividing net income by the total number of fully‑diluted shares:

\[
\text{EPS} = \frac{\text{Net Income}}{\text{Fully Diluted Shares}} 
          = \frac{\$2{,}000{,}000}{50{,}000}
          = \$40 \text{ per share}
\]

So the EPS would be **$40 per share**.

